      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" These fields were used inconsistently across teams\u2014Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant while Payments Ops used department=payments. This inconsistency caused ingestion normalization issues and routing failures in the Rules Engine because the tenant configuration did not collapse these variants into a single canonical attribute.\n\nJin proposed a fast fix to avoid waiting on Okta change control: add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) to produce a normalized field for the correlator. This is a configuration-only, hot-reloadable change that can be applied quickly without requiring Okta flow changes, thus avoiding the 2\u20134 week delay associated with Okta change control. This fix can be deployed by pushing the mapping rule and enabling SCIM trace probes targeting non-peak nodes, with no full appliance restart needed\u2014only a collector process restart on non-settlement nodes if necessary.\n\nThis approach provides immediate normalization and diagnostic visibility while a longer-term standardization at the identity source (Okta) is planned but delayed by change control processes. [art_79f625aafa16] [art_545110f843dc]",
