      ],
      "answer": "Yes, there is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts, not just MapleBridge. The customers affected by this pattern include:\n\n- MapleBridge Insurance  \n- MapleFork Franchise Systems  \n- MapleWest Bank  \n- MapleBay Marketplace  \n- Maple Regional Transit Authority  \n- MaplePath Career Institute  \n- City of Verdant Bay  \n\nThe shared failure pattern in plain English is:\n\nAfter migration from legacy workflow tooling, approval workflows for Canada-specific policies fail because global-default rules override or bypass region-specific (province or country) approval rules. This happens due to incorrect rule evaluation precedence where global-default policies are evaluated with higher priority than province or country overrides. Additionally, schema key mismatches (e.g., 'country_code' vs 'country') and delayed schema registry synchronization across evaluation clusters exacerbate the problem. As a result, approval playbooks skip approver nodes, approvals get stuck or auto-denied, or approvals route incorrectly to global approvers instead of Canada-specific approvers. This leads to automated approvals being bypassed or blocked, requiring manual overrides and causing compliance and operational risks.\n\nSupporting details per customer:\n\n- MapleBridge Insurance: Canada-specific approval gating bypassed due to conflict between 'canada.v2' overrides and 'global.v3' default rule caused by delayed schema sync. [art_f4a8c516b934, art_54e35e2cb431, art_e697b3abe158]  \n- MapleFork Franchise Systems: Region override ignored; global-default evaluated last with higher precedence causing blocked automated approvals. [art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_ad58f3ce1afd]  \n- MapleWest Bank: Approvals routed to global approver group instead of Canada approvers due to schema key mismatch and rule precedence bug. [art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_3db205cb21ca]  \n- MapleBay Marketplace: Approvals stuck or auto-denied due to global-default priority higher than country override. [art_39c1434aa40a]  \n- Maple Regional Transit Authority: Approvals stuck in queue for Ontario and Quebec routes due to precedence bug where global-default overrides region-specific predicates. [art_6be1b68b59cb]  \n- MaplePath Career Institute: Dropped approvals correlated with ruleset version and country_default override causing global override to short-circuit province allow. [art_981952a71434]  \n- City of Verdant Bay: Approval playbooks skipping approver nodes due to incorrect policy lookup order prioritizing global_default over province and city overrides. [art_cbfb5f92862c]  \n\nTherefore, MapleBridge is not a one-off case; this approval-bypass pattern recurs across multiple Canadian accounts with a common root cause in rule evaluation precedence and schema normalization issues after migration from legacy tooling. [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_e697b3abe158, art_3db205cb21ca]",
